From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:10:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep MLO radio indices in WSI topology order

Multiple PCIe chips join an MLO group in asynchronous probe order. That
order currently selects userspace radio indices and the wiphy identity.
On SBE1V1K a reboot changes the band belonging to a persisted radio index,
so otherwise valid AP configurations fail to set beacon parameters.

Sort the pdev map by the device tree WSI index before allocating an MLO
wiphy. Preserve the order of pdevs within a chip and leave internal device
and firmware link IDs unchanged. Non-MLO enumeration is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -15815,6 +15815,24 @@
 	ab->free_vdev_map = (1LL << total_vdev) - 1;
 }
 
+static void ath12k_mac_sort_pdevs(struct ath12k_pdev_map *pdev_map, u8 num_pdevs)
+{
+	struct ath12k_pdev_map pdev;
+	int i, j;
+
+	/* PCI probe order is asynchronous. Keep the userspace radio indices and
+	 * wiphy identity in WSI topology order without changing firmware IDs.
+	 * The stable sort also preserves pdev order within each chip.
+	 */
+	for (i = 1; i < num_pdevs; i++) {
+		pdev = pdev_map[i];
+		for (j = i; j > 0 &&
+		     pdev_map[j - 1].ab->wsi_info.index > pdev.ab->wsi_info.index; j--)
+			pdev_map[j] = pdev_map[j - 1];
+		pdev_map[j] = pdev;
+	}
+}
+
 int ath12k_mac_allocate(struct ath12k_hw_group *ag)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pdev_map pdev_map[ATH12K_GROUP_MAX_RADIO];
@@ -15890,6 +15908,9 @@
 			}
 		}
 
+		if (ag->mlo_capable)
+			ath12k_mac_sort_pdevs(pdev_map, radio_per_hw);
+
 		ab = pdev_map->ab;
 
 		ah = ath12k_mac_hw_allocate(ag, pdev_map, radio_per_hw);
